## Vendor Invoice Processing — Architectural Plan

**What the flow does:** When a new PDF appears in your SharePoint folder, the flow triggers automatically, downloads the file, runs it through the IxP extraction model, maps the fields to a SAP payload, and posts it — no humans, no stops.

---

```mermaid
graph LR
    trigger(SharePoint File Created)
    downloadFile[Download File from SharePoint]
    extractInvoice[Extract Invoice Fields]
    mapFields[Map Fields to SAP Format]
    postToSap[Post to SAP mock]
    doneSuccess(Done)
    doneExtractErr(Done Extraction Error)
    doneSapErr(Done SAP Error)
    trigger -->|output| downloadFile
    downloadFile -->|output| extractInvoice
    downloadFile -->|error| doneExtractErr
    extractInvoice -->|success| mapFields
    extractInvoice -->|error| doneExtractErr
    mapFields -->|success| postToSap
    mapFields -->|error| doneSapErr
    postToSap -->|output| doneSuccess
```

---

### Nodes

| # | Name | Type | Notes |
|---|------|------|-------|
| 1 | SharePoint File Created | Connector trigger (`uipath-microsoft-onedrive`) | Fires when a new file lands in the folder. Connection ✅ ready. |
| 2 | Download File from SharePoint | Connector activity (`download-file`) | Fetches the PDF bytes. Same connection. |
| 3 | Extract Invoice Fields | IxP extraction node | Runs your invoice model, returns structured fields. |
| 4 | Map Fields to SAP Format | Script node | Translates `Fields[]` array into a flat SAP payload object. |
| 5 | Post to SAP | **Mock** (placeholder) | Replaced with real SAP connector once a connection exists. |
| 6–8 | Done / Error ends | End nodes | One for success, two for errors. |

