Everything else about that node — the auth mode, the field mapping, the error handling — is already done.

---

**4. What "valid and formatted" actually means.**

`validate` runs the same Zod schema checks the platform uses at publish time — node types exist in the registry, all required inputs are present, all cross-node references (`$vars.*`) have matching variable declarations, error ports are only used on nodes where `errorHandlingEnabled: true`, and the bindings are internally consistent. **It catches structural and schema errors before deployment.**

What it does *not* check: whether your SAP URL actually responds, whether the InvoiceIXP model will correctly extract a given invoice, or whether extracted field names like `VendorName` match what your specific model taxonomy uses. Those only surface when the flow runs against a real invoice — which is why I'd recommend dropping a test PDF into the **New Vendor** folder after you fill in the SAP URL, before you declare it production-ready.

